-- title:
--   Injectivity of a Z-chart factorisation of the generic point
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring that is an integral domain and Noetherian, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$ satisfying `IsElliptic`. Write $E = \mathrm{Proj}$ of the grading on $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,3)\,R$ modulo the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of `W.toProjective`, with structure morphism $E \to \operatorname{Spec} R$. The statement first installs, as local instances, smoothness of this structure morphism (from relative dimension $1$), its geometric integrality (obtained from the compatibility of the projective model with base change to fields), and hence integrality of $E$ as a locally Noetherian scheme; it then endows the function field $K(E)$ with the $R$-algebra structure coming from the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_{E,\eta} \to E$ at the generic point $\eta$ followed by the structure morphism. The assertion is: for every $R$-algebra homomorphism $\psi$ from the degree-zero homogeneous localisation of the graded quotient away from the class of $X_2$ (the $Z$-chart ring $\mathcal A_2$) to $K(E)$, if the canonical morphism $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_{E,\eta} \to E$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\psi$ followed by the open immersion of the index-$2$ member of the affine open cover of $E$, then $\psi$ is injective as a function.
--
--   This is the standard fact that restriction to the stalk at the generic point of an integral scheme is injective on the sections over an affine open, specialised to the $Z$-chart of the projective Weierstrass model. It supplies the injectivity needed to transfer relations from $K(E)$ back to the chart ring $\mathcal A_2$, and is used in [`WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_genericPoint_zChart_addMap_self_ne_zeroClass`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.kw_ev_genericPoint_zChart_addMap_self_ne_zeroClass).
-- source:
